==============================================================================
DOES THE U-SPECTRUM SEE THE FLIP-RANK EXCESS?   (n, structural facts)
==============================================================================
 n  |G_n|  V_merged  #SC rho(flip) ceil_log2  excess
 3      2         2    2         1         1       0
 4      4         3    2         2         2       0
 5     12        10    8         4         4       0
 6     56        34   12         7         6       1
  (excess first appears at n=6; HYP-3810: SC classes carry it)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
n = 3
  |G_n|=2, #SC=2, V_merged=2
  (1) distinct skew-spectra = 1;  distinct U-spectra = 1  (equal => Cayley is a spectral bijection, U carries no more)
  (2) resolution ceiling V_merged=2: distinct-spectra 1 < V_merged (LOSES 1 MORE beyond complement-pairs)
      cospectral collisions = |G_n|-distinct = 1  (>= #NS-pairs = 0 forced by complement-reflection)
  (3) 2nd moment trace(S^2): values=[-6.0]  (constant = -n(n-1) = -6 => BLIND)
      4th moment trace(S^4): #distinct values = 1  (first informative even moment)
      circular trace(U)=sum cos(theta): #distinct values = 1  (Cayley wrap makes the blind 2nd moment informative; note it matches/beats trace(S^4))
  (4) COMBINATORIAL: #distinct H(Redei) = 2, #distinct (H,c3) = 2  (vs #distinct spectra = 1) -- combinatorial counts resolve FAR more than any spectrum
      H all odd (Redei) = True; metagraph 2nd moment Var(H) = 1.000  (THM-589 W(n); the SECOND MOMENT that IS relevant to covering/flip-rank)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
n = 4
  |G_n|=4, #SC=2, V_merged=3
  (1) distinct skew-spectra = 2;  distinct U-spectra = 2  (equal => Cayley is a spectral bijection, U carries no more)
  (2) resolution ceiling V_merged=3: distinct-spectra 2 < V_merged (LOSES 1 MORE beyond complement-pairs)
      cospectral collisions = |G_n|-distinct = 2  (>= #NS-pairs = 1 forced by complement-reflection)
  (3) 2nd moment trace(S^2): values=[-12.0]  (constant = -n(n-1) = -12 => BLIND)
      4th moment trace(S^4): #distinct values = 2  (first informative even moment)
      circular trace(U)=sum cos(theta): #distinct values = 2  (Cayley wrap makes the blind 2nd moment informative; note it matches/beats trace(S^4))
  (4) COMBINATORIAL: #distinct H(Redei) = 3, #distinct (H,c3) = 3  (vs #distinct spectra = 2) -- combinatorial counts resolve FAR more than any spectrum
      H all odd (Redei) = True; metagraph 2nd moment Var(H) = 2.000  (THM-589 W(n); the SECOND MOMENT that IS relevant to covering/flip-rank)

