  |G_n|=12, #SC=8, V_merged=10
  (1) distinct skew-spectra = 2;  distinct U-spectra = 2  (equal => Cayley is a spectral bijection, U carries no more)
  (2) resolution ceiling V_merged=10: distinct-spectra 2 < V_merged (LOSES 8 MORE beyond complement-pairs)
      cospectral collisions = |G_n|-distinct = 10  (>= #NS-pairs = 2 forced by complement-reflection)
  (3) 2nd moment trace(S^2): values=[-20.0]  (constant = -n(n-1) = -20 => BLIND)
      4th moment trace(S^4): #distinct values = 2  (first informative even moment)
      circular trace(U)=sum cos(theta): #distinct values = 2  (Cayley wrap makes the blind 2nd moment informative; note it matches/beats trace(S^4))
  (4) COMBINATORIAL: #distinct H(Redei) = 7, #distinct (H,c3) = 8  (vs #distinct spectra = 2) -- combinatorial counts resolve FAR more than any spectrum
